  "qualification": "Full all-feature HyperBREP tests and release retained-parameter regressions pass. Hypercurve chart integration and parameter-module tests pass. Both crates pass strict all-target/all-feature Clippy and warning-denied rustdoc; BREP WASM library build, fuzz-bin strict Clippy, both formatting checks and three release benchmark builds pass. Six kernel processes preserve all 66 receipts; three executions each of the retained and work-budget harnesses preserve their four exact-assertion rows.",
  "source_review": "Parameter reuses opaque admitted BezierParameter2 authority and exposes a stored-Real view plus strict fallible comparison. Spatial projection candidates retain roots, verify all three coordinates at the same selector, then reuse existing affine chart transport for NURBS domains. Topology consumers explicitly report their remaining materialization boundary. Spatial inverse helpers move to geometry/location.rs. No new polynomial/root algorithm or compatibility path is introduced.",
  "setup_corrections": "The first upstream parameter filter selected zero tests and is excluded. The corrected bezier_parameter:: filter must report a nonzero test count. The initial all-feature Clippy run could not download an uncached locked optional dependency under --offline; an approved network retry populated the cache, and the final offline check succeeds. Setup logs are retained separately.",
  "limits": [
    "WP02 and G1 are incomplete: no retained 3D point evaluation, selected edge-domain split with dual pcurves, transform or selected graph archive/reload composition.",
    "Partly constant NURBS preimages remain a typed unsupported result. Comparisons that cannot be certified remain errors; arbitrary coefficient-field or singular-branch completeness is not claimed.",
    "Only existing instrumented root refinements and promotions share OperationContext limits. Full scalar/geometry/degree/coefficient/memory/time accounting is still open.",
    "New retained-query timing rows measure capabilities absent from the baseline; they are not matched speedup comparisons. The work-budget harness changes only its exact-result assertion for the new API and is not used for a cross-revision timing claim.",
    "Kernel timing and whole-process RSS samples are descriptive, with no allocation-count, asymptotic-growth or statistical-significance claim.",
    "WASM and fuzz targets compile; no WASM execution, independent external geometry oracle, new fuzz/lexicase/ASan campaign, full-workspace or pre-push qualification is claimed."
  ],
